<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marcus Lollius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 2 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marcus Lollius was a Roman politician and general, consul in 21 BCE and a close associate of Augustus. In 16 BCE, as governor in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, he was defeated by the Sugambri, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/usipetes">Usipetes</a> and Tencteri, who captured the eagle of the Fifth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a>, a disaster known as the clades Lolliana. He later advised Augustus's grandson Gaius Caesar in the East.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marcus-lollius.jpg" alt="Marcus Lollius" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlomorino · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ponte_fabricio03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
